@page "/"

<PageTitle>FlociLab</PageTitle>

<h1>FlociLab</h1>

<p class="lede">
    The same operation, run against four cloud emulators with four official SDKs, on one screen.
    Every sample is a Razor Class Library with exactly one cloud package, so it can be lifted out
    and run on its own.
</p>

<h2>Where things stand</h2>

<p>
    The spine is up: contracts, endpoint configuration for all four providers, Aspire orchestration
    and the coverage matrix. No service demos are registered yet — those start with object storage
    across all four clouds.
</p>

<p>
    <a class="button" href="/coverage">Open the coverage matrix →</a>
</p>

<h2>The emulators</h2>

<table class="grid">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Cloud</th>
            <th>Image</th>
            <th>Endpoint</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td>AWS</td><td><code>floci/floci</code></td><td><code>http://127.0.0.1:4566</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Azure</td><td><code>floci/floci-az</code></td><td><code>http://127.0.0.1:4577</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>GCP</td><td><code>floci/floci-gcp</code></td><td><code>http://127.0.0.1:4588</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>OCI</td><td><code>floci/floci-oci</code></td><td><code>http://127.0.0.1:4599</code></td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<p class="note">
    The AppHost also starts the <a href="http://127.0.0.1:4500" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Floci
    web console</a> on port 4500 — a separate product, and AWS/Azure/GCP only. This app is the OCI
    story, and the side-by-side one.
</p>

<p class="note">
    Endpoints come from the <code>Floci</code> configuration section. Running under the Aspire
    AppHost overrides them with the live container endpoints; running inside the Compose network
    means setting <code>Floci__Aws__Endpoint=http://floci:4566</code> and friends.
</p>
